1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,860
In sixteen sixty-five, a terrible plague

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,500
swept through England. To keep students

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:07,860
safe, the university at Cambridge closed

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,240
its doors, and a young student called

5
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,920
Isaac Newton went home to his family's

6
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:15,220
farmhouse in the village of Woolsthorpe.

7
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,220
He had been born in that same house on

8
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:21,300
Christmas Day, sixteen forty-two. His

9
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:23,260
father had died a few months before.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,940
Newton was so tiny, his mother later said,

11
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,260
that he could have fitted inside a quart

12
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:29,840
pot.

13
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,000
For almost two years, he worked alone. He

14
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,480
studied light, invented new kinds of

15
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:39,280
mathematics, and asked questions no one

16
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,280
had asked before.

17
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,780
Many years later, when he was an old man,

18
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,180
Newton told a friend how one of those

19
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,320
questions began.

20
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:50,660
He was sitting in the garden thinking when

21
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,320
an apple fell from a tree.

22
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,300
The apple didn't hit him on the head. That

23
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:57,580
part was added later, but it made him

24
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,000
wonder.

25
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,180
The apple always falls straight down

26
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,820
towards the center of the Earth. The pull

27
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:05,980
that drags it down works at the top of the

28
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,780
tree. It works at the top of a tall tower

29
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,600
and at the top of a mountain.

30
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,060
So how far up does it reach?

31
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,660
Could it reach all the way to the Moon?

32
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:19,880
It was an extraordinary idea. If the Earth

33
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,200
was pulling on the Moon, then the Moon

34
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:24,660
should be falling. But it was still up

35
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:27,580
there night after night. So what was

36
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:28,380
holding it up?
